(a) Creation. There shall be a department within the city's government created known as the "Lovejoy Community Recreation Department." The department shall be responsible for the following:
(1) Operation of the center;
(2) Planning and execution of recreational and other community-oriented programs to benefit the citizens of the city;
(3) Planning and execution of programs designed to benefit the youth and the senior citizens of the city;
(4) Such other duties as are designed to deliver services to the city's citizens through education, recreation, or community service.
(b) Budget.
(1) There shall be a separate account established for the department within the city budget. The account shall contain an expenditures component and a revenue component.
(2) All revenues and incomes received by the city derived from the rental of the center, community or recreational activities conducted by the department, donations, grants, and other contributions to the city intended for recreational and community use shall be placed in the revenue account of the department's budget and shall not be expended for the purposes not related to the department's duties and business. Nothing in this section shall prohibit the mayor and council or their designee from the use of any physical asset of the department for other official city use on a temporary basis. Nothing contained herein shall prevent the mayor and council from providing additional funding from authorized sources to the department.
(c) Supervision of department.
(1) Appointment; duties and responsibilities.
a. The mayor and council may appoint a director of community recreation. In the absence of said appointment, supervision of the department shall be provided for as the mayor and council may direct or pursuant to other ordinances and the city's Charter. The director shall direct the operations of the department and shall have the following duties and responsibilities:
1. Supervision of department employees, including recommendations on personnel action to the mayor and council;
2. Management of the center and such other facilities dedicated to community recreation that the city may own or operate;
3. Receipt, maintenance and accounting of the funds and assets of the department; forwarding of all funds and revenues to the proper city official as may be prescribed by the mayor and council;
4. Such other duties and responsibilities that may be prescribed by the mayor and council or their designee.
b. The mayor and council shall create a job description for the director, outlining in reasonable specificity the duties and responsibilities of that position.
(2) Advisors for special programs. There shall be created a position of advisor for senior citizen programs and a position of advisor for youth programs. The advisors shall provide to the administrative assistant, mayor and council information concerning programs of the department concerning senior citizens and youth. The advisors shall act as a liaison between the city and persons concerned with such programs. The mayor and council may, by resolution, create such other advisory positions as they relate to other special programs by the department. Ay such advisors shall be compensated in the amount of $50.00 per calendar month in order to assist in defraying expenses on the part of the advisors.
(3) The mayor and council may create and fund such other positions as are deemed necessary and proper within the department.
(Ord. No. 2006-05, art. I, § 2, 6-13-2006; Ord. No. 06, pt. III(art. I, § 2), 6-9-2008)
